  <dashboards>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 4'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.1: Which department generates the highest treatment cost?   </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Based on the empirical data visualized in the Q4: Department Performance bar chart, the Neurology department generates the highest cumulative treatment cost, yielding an aggregate expenditure of 5,320,474.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.2: Which region has more critical patients?   </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>By analyzing the Q6: Outcome Analysis chart alongside the Q3: Patient Distribution geographic breakdown, the total critical patient count across the hospital network stands at 84. When interactive dashboard filter actions are applied by clicking the &quot;Critical&quot; slice, the data reveals that the North region carries the highest relative volume of severe case profiles, closely followed by the South.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.3: What business decisions can hospital management take from these insights?   </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Clinical Asset &amp; Personnel Realignment: Management should initiate a strategic resource reallocation, routing specialized critical care assets, emergency ventilation hardware, and additional intensive care staff directly to the North regional facility to properly support its disproportionately high volume of severe clinical cases.  </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Targeted Expenditure Auditing: Because the Neurology division operates as the primary cost driver across the hospital network (surpassing 5.3M), administrators should conduct a targeted clinical operations audit. This should focus on examining hardware utilization, reviewing specialized pharmaceutical procurement contracts, and optimizing clinical workflows to eliminate waste without lowering the quality of patient care.  </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Capacity &amp; Operational Optimization: Management can use the overall patient volumes across regions (with the West leading the total patient distribution) to balance staff scheduling. This ensures high-volume regions are never understaffed, while lower-volume regions like Central do not experience costly over-staffing bottlenecks.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='6' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98000' id='5' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.1: Which department generates the highest treatment cost?   </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Based on the empirical data visualized in the Q4: Department Performance bar chart, the Neurology department generates the highest cumulative treatment cost, yielding an aggregate expenditure of 5,320,474.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.2: Which region has more critical patients?   </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>By analyzing the Q6: Outcome Analysis chart alongside the Q3: Patient Distribution geographic breakdown, the total critical patient count across the hospital network stands at 84. When interactive dashboard filter actions are applied by clicking the &quot;Critical&quot; slice, the data reveals that the North region carries the highest relative volume of severe case profiles, closely followed by the South.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>10.3: What business decisions can hospital management take from these insights?   </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Clinical Asset &amp; Personnel Realignment: Management should initiate a strategic resource reallocation, routing specialized critical care assets, emergency ventilation hardware, and additional intensive care staff directly to the North regional facility to properly support its disproportionately high volume of severe clinical cases.  </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Targeted Expenditure Auditing: Because the Neurology division operates as the primary cost driver across the hospital network (surpassing 5.3M), administrators should conduct a targeted clinical operations audit. This should focus on examining hardware utilization, reviewing specialized pharmaceutical procurement contracts, and optimizing clinical workflows to eliminate waste without lowering the quality of patient care.  </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Capacity &amp; Operational Optimization: Management can use the overall patient volumes across regions (with the West leading the total patient distribution) to balance staff scheduling. This ensures high-volume regions are never understaffed, while lower-volume regions like Central do not experience costly over-staffing bottlenecks.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
