    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Q2'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q2: What are Actions in Tableau? Explain how Filter Action can help hospital management analyze patient data. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Actions in Tableau:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Actions are the interactive elements that make dashboards dynamic. They allow you to add context and interactivity by connecting your visualizations. The main types of actions are Filter, Highlight, Go to URL, Go to Sheet, Change Parameter, and Change Set Values.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Filter Action for Hospital Management:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> A Filter Action sends information between worksheets. If hospital management is looking at a dashboard containing a map of clinics and a bar chart of patient wait times, a Filter Action allows them to click on a specific clinic on the map. Instantly, the wait time bar chart updates to show </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>only</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> the data for that selected clinic. This prevents them from having to build separate dashboards for every single location.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='10' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='9' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q2: What are Actions in Tableau? Explain how Filter Action can help hospital management analyze patient data. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Actions in Tableau:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Actions are the interactive elements that make dashboards dynamic. They allow you to add context and interactivity by connecting your visualizations. The main types of actions are Filter, Highlight, Go to URL, Go to Sheet, Change Parameter, and Change Set Values.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Filter Action for Hospital Management:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> A Filter Action sends information between worksheets. If hospital management is looking at a dashboard containing a map of clinics and a bar chart of patient wait times, a Filter Action allows them to click on a specific clinic on the map. Instantly, the wait time bar chart updates to show </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>only</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> the data for that selected clinic. This prevents them from having to build separate dashboards for every single location.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{73807C2A-8E5C-49E1-AE00-AD82A9448148}' />
    </dashboard>
